<!--
  Per-culture default BodyProperties for the Character Creation screen.

  Format:
    <Culture id="<culture_string_id>">
      <BodyProperties version="4" key="<128-hex-char-key>" />
    </Culture>

  - Paste the BodyProperties XML element exactly as produced by the in-game
    BodyProperties.ToString() (or copied from a save / face-customizer export).
  - The key must be exactly 128 hex characters; otherwise the entry is skipped
    with a warning in taom_debug_*.log.
  - Optional weight / build attributes on <BodyProperties .../> are honoured if
    present; absent values default to weight=0 build=0 (vanilla parser default).
  - The `age` attribute is parsed by vanilla but NOT applied to the player —
    Hero.Age is computed from BirthDay, which we do not touch. Including age=
    has no visible effect.
  - Cultures not listed here fall back to the vanilla per-culture random body.
  - The provider is a Singleton: edits to this file require restarting Bannerlord,
    not just reloading a save.

  TAOM culture-id reference (see spcultures.xslt + taom_spcultures.xml):
    vlandia    → Rohan        (XSLT-modified vanilla Vlandia)
    empire     → Dunland      (XSLT-modified vanilla Empire)
    battania   → Khand        (XSLT-modified vanilla Battania)
    aserai     → Harad        (XSLT-modified vanilla Aserai)
    sturgia    → Barding      (XSLT-modified vanilla Sturgia)
    khuzait   → Rhun         (XSLT-modified vanilla Khuzait)
    mordor, gondor, erebor, mirkwood, lothlorien, rivendell,
    dolguldur, gundabad, isengard, umbar, dale     → TAOM custom cultures
-->
